---@class aws.gameliftstreams.StartStreamSessionInput
---@field ClientToken? aws.gameliftstreams.ClientToken A unique identifier that represents a client request. The request is idempotent, which ensures that an API request completes only once. When users send a request, Amazon GameLift Streams automatically populates this field.
---@field Description? aws.gameliftstreams.Description A human-readable label for the stream session. You can update this value later.
---@field Identifier aws.gameliftstreams.Identifier The stream group to run this stream session with.
---@field Protocol aws.gameliftstreams.Protocol|string The data transport protocol to use for the stream session.
---@field SignalRequest aws.gameliftstreams.SignalRequest|distilled.Secret A WebRTC ICE offer string to use when initializing a WebRTC connection. Typically, the offer is a very long JSON string. Provide the string as a text value in quotes.
---@field ApplicationIdentifier aws.gameliftstreams.Identifier An Amazon Resource Name (ARN) or ID that uniquely identifies the application resource. Example ARN: arn:aws:gameliftstreams:us-west-2:111122223333:application/a-9ZY8X7Wv6. Example ID: a-9ZY8X7Wv6.
---@field UserId? aws.gameliftstreams.UserId An opaque, unique identifier for an end-user, defined by the developer.
---@field Locations? aws.gameliftstreams.LocationList A list of locations, in order of priority, where you want Amazon GameLift Streams to start a stream from. For example, us-east-1. Amazon GameLift Streams selects the location with the next available capacity to start a single stream session in. If this value is empty, Amazon GameLift Streams attempts to start a stream session in the primary location.
---@field ConnectionTimeoutSeconds? aws.gameliftstreams.ConnectionTimeoutSeconds Length of time (in seconds) that Amazon GameLift Streams should wait for a client to connect or reconnect to the stream session. Applies to both connection and reconnection scenarios. This time span starts when the stream session reaches ACTIVE state. If no client connects before the timeout, Amazon GameLift Streams terminates the stream session. Default value is 120.
---@field SessionLengthSeconds? aws.gameliftstreams.SessionLengthSeconds The maximum duration of a session. Amazon GameLift Streams will automatically terminate a session after this amount of time has elapsed, regardless of any existing client connections. Default value is 43200 (12 hours).
---@field AdditionalLaunchArgs? aws.gameliftstreams.GameLaunchArgList A list of CLI arguments that are sent to the streaming server when a stream session launches. You can use this to configure the application or stream session details. You can also provide custom arguments that Amazon GameLift Streams passes to your game client.
---@field AdditionalEnvironmentVariables? aws.gameliftstreams.EnvironmentVariables A set of options that you can use to control the stream session runtime environment, expressed as a set of key-value pairs. You can use this to configure the application or stream session details. You can also provide custom environment variables that Amazon GameLift Streams passes to your game client.
---@field PerformanceStatsConfiguration? aws.gameliftstreams.PerformanceStatsConfiguration Configuration settings for sharing the stream session's performance stats with the client
---@field RoleArn? aws.gameliftstreams.IamRoleArn|distilled.Secret The ARN of an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that Amazon GameLift Streams assumes on your behalf during the stream session. The role grants Amazon GameLift Streams permission to obtain temporary credentials for your application. The role's trust policy must allow the gameliftstreams.amazonaws.com service principal to assume it. The role name must start with GameLiftStreams-.
---@field DisplayConfiguration? aws.gameliftstreams.DisplayConfiguration The configuration for the stream session's virtual monitor, including the resolution settings.

